| Some utility words related to setting up the clock[s] on the CH32V.
| These were copied from target/ARM/stm32/; only the register names had to
| be changed!

loading CH32V clock setting

hex
__meta

| Set a byte register to a value (set), then loop, reading the same
| register, until the register anded with a mask matches the match value.

: set-until-match  ( set mask match reg)
   >r  rot r@ c!  ( set reg to "set" value)
   begin  over r@ c@ and  over =  until  r>  drop drop drop ;

| We do this because we don't have a multiply instruction on the ch32v003!
: 5*  dup 2 << + ;

| NOTE: sysclk! sets HPRE (the AHB clock prescaler) to /1. The HPRE field
| is the high 4 bits of the low byte of RCC_CFGR0.

: sysclk!  ( clksrc)  0f  over 5*  RCC_CFGR0  set-until-match ;

: >hsi   0 ( SW=HSI) sysclk! ;
: >hse   1 ( SW=HSE) sysclk! ;
: >pll   2 ( SW=PLL) sysclk! ;

: hse-start   ( hsebits)  2 2  [ RCC_CTLR 2 + #]  set-until-match ;
: +hse         1 ( HSEON)           hse-start ;
: +hse-bypass  5 ( HSEON + HSEBYP)  hse-start ;

: +pll   1  2 2  [ RCC_CTLR 3 + #]  set-until-match ;
: -pll   0  2 0  [ RCC_CTLR 3 + #]  set-until-match ;
